  "findings": [
    "The multi-architecture build's sm_120a code runs on a real RTX 5090 (Blackwell): every run completed, finite, non-silent, 48 kHz stereo, not truncated",
    "Short song 8.5 s and full song 30.2-30.4 s (four runs), versus 14.3 s and 37.7 s on the Windows RTX 4090; peak GPU use above idle 5.4-5.5 GB",
    "Outputs are identical across processes on Linux, but the Linux short take is a different rendition (46.0 s of audio) from Windows (66.4 s) with the same seed; FEATURES.md already allows backend differences",
    "cuBLAS loaded only from the pinned NVIDIA pack, but libcudart.so.13.3.29 still came from the toolkit: the Linux build links the CUDA runtime dynamically, unlike Windows. The Linux runtime folder therefore also needs libcudart, now pinned as cudart-13.3.29-linux-x64 (1.6 MB archive)",
    "The engine's RUNPATH is the absolute build folder; packaging must set an $ORIGIN-relative RUNPATH",
    "Forced termination exited within 0.14 s at every stage and released GPU memory within 0.2 s with no leftover files",
    "Final-write sweep: kills up to 40 ms left no WAV (at most the three small files); runs at 80 ms and later had already finished. No truncated WAV was captured on Linux this time",
    "First attempt stopped after a successful build because yue-synth --help exits 1 under set -e; fixed in the kit (PR #17) and rerun reusing the build"
  ],
